      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) in the given diagram, we need to use the fact that the sum of the angles around a point is \\( 360^\\circ \\). The angles given in the diagram are \\( 4x^\\circ \\), \\( 5x^\\circ \\), \\( 2x^\\circ \\), and \\( x^\\circ \\). These angles form a full circle around a point, so we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n4x + 5x + 2x + x = 360^\\circ\n\\]\n\nCombining the terms on the left side, we get:\n\n\\[\n12x = 360^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 12:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{360^\\circ}{12} = 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).",
